# GuessWatts: copy guide

This guide owns the voice and the glossary. The code owns the strings: `index.html`, `sobre.html`,
`index.md`, `sobre.md` and `js/*.js` (the status line in `STATUS` in `js/main.js`, the result
verdicts and subtitles in `js/ui-renderer.js`). To change what a person reads, change it there,
following this guide and the nine rules in `.claude/rules/copy.md`.

Every Portuguese line below is an example of the voice, marked as one. A "Quote" is copied from the
code and names where it lives; when the code changes, update the quote or drop it. An
"Illustration" is not in the product and only shows the tone.

---

## Voice

### Who we are

A neighbour who understands electricity and wants to help. We are not an energy company, we sell
nothing and take no commission. We only want people to stop paying too much.

### Principles

| Principle | Means | Does not mean |
|---|---|---|
| Friendly | Close, approachable, human | Childish, exclamatory, forced |
| Honest | Open about limits; shows the number a verdict rests on | Defensive, full of disclaimers |
| Direct | Gets to the point | Curt, cold, robotic |
| Useful | Says what to do next | Lecturing, patronising |

### Address

"Tu" throughout, never "você", never mixed in one screen.

Illustration: "Quanto pagas de luz?", not "Quanto paga de luz?"

### What we avoid

| Pattern | Illustration | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Empty superlatives | "A melhor solução!" | No credibility |
| Artificial urgency | "Muda já!" | Manipulative |
| Exclamation marks | "Incrível!!" | Reads as spam |
| Unexplained jargon | "kWh em período de vazio" | Shuts people out; explain beside it (copy rule 2) |
| Diminutives | "É só um cliquezinho" | Condescending |
| Decorative emoji | "Poupa já! 🚀💰" | Visual noise |
| Marketing speak | "Oferta imperdível" | Breeds distrust |
| Legal boilerplate | "Os valores apresentados são meramente indicativos..." | Hides the point; say what the estimate rests on instead |

### Tone by context

| Context | Tone | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Opening question | Curious, inviting | Quote, `index.html` hero: "Quanto pagas de eletricidade por mês?" |
| Input | Calm, clear | Quote, `index.html`: "Arrasta a tua fatura em PDF para aqui, ou" |
| Result | Direct, with its basis | Quote, `js/ui-renderer.js` (Estimado subtitle): "Estimativa a partir de uma fatura de 80 €: tarifa simples, 4,6 kVA e o consumo que esse valor paga numa oferta típica." |
| Instructions | Confident, step by step | Quote, `index.html`: "Mudar é gratuito e o novo fornecedor trata de tudo: não precisas de avisar o atual." |
| Errors | Says what happened and what to do next (copy rule 3) | Quote, `js/main.js` `STATUS`: "Não conseguimos ler esta fatura. Podes introduzir os valores à mão." |
| Confirmations | Neutral, minimal | Illustration: "Link copiado" |

### A verdict shows its number

Copy rule 9. A result that says "no switch needed" shows the saving or the prices it compares, so
the 1 €/month threshold (`GOOD_TARIFF_MARGIN` in `js/ui-renderer.js`) never reads as a hidden rule.

Quote, `resultVerdict` in `js/ui-renderer.js` (Preciso, saving above 0 and up to 1 €/month):
"Poupas 0,80 €/mês. É pouco para compensar a mudança: já tens uma boa tarifa."

Quote, same function (Estimado, bill within 1 €/month of the cheapest offer):
"A tua fatura (20,00 €/mês) já está ao nível da oferta mais barata (21,46 €/mês): já tens uma boa
tarifa."

Not: "Já tens uma boa tarifa." on its own.

"Poupas" appears only in Preciso, against the person's current supplier. Estimado describes the
market instead (ADR-011), so its button is "Comparar", not "Ver quanto perco".

### Rhetoric, sparingly

Classic devices that work without sounding like a salesperson. All illustrations.

- Antithesis, to contrast now and possible: "Pagas 95 €. Podias pagar 71 €."
- Tricolon, for rhythm: "Sem contratos. Sem papelada. Sem complicações."
- Litotes, more credible than an absolute: "Não é complicado", not "É super fácil".
- Rhetorical question, inviting without pressing: "Quanto pagas de luz por mês?"

### Numbers and sources

- Numbers in PT-PT form through `formatEuro` and `formatNumber` (copy rule 6).
- A market figure always names its source and month, and comes from data the site ships
  (`data/`); never invent one. Illustration: "Fonte: ERSE, junho de 2026".
- The price date comes from `data/meta.json` and is written by `js/data-date.js`; the copy never
  promises an update frequency.

