## Facts the copy relies on

### Switching supplier

What the switch guide (`#result-info-template` in `index.html`) tells people:

- Switching is free and the new supplier handles it; the person does not contact the old one.
- It takes up to 3 weeks (ERSE, Síntese Mensal, June 2026; not re-checked in this guide).
- A contract with fidelização may carry an exit cost; the person checks the bill for the end date.
- The new supplier asks for: CPE, NIF, morada, telefone, leitura do contador, and the IBAN when
  paying by direct debit.

### Changing the tariff option (simples, bi-horária, tri-horária)

Checked on 2026-10-21 against ERSE's official texts.

Article 51 of ERSE's Regulamento de Relações Comerciais (RRC) sets a 12-month permanence for a
network-access tariff option. The Regulamento Tarifário do setor elétrico for the 2026-2029
regulatory period (Regulamento n.º 1218/2025, Diário da República, 2.ª série, n.º 216, 7 November
2025; rectified by Declaração de Retificação n.º 17/2026/2, 7 January 2026), article 54, n.º 5,
limits that permanence, for supplies up to 20,7 kVA, to the ciclo de contagem (the daily or weekly
cycle). ERSE's press release of 13 October 2025 states the effect: a BTN consumer up to 20,7 kVA
can change between simples, bi-horária and tri-horária at any time, and the 12-month permanence
ends.

For the copy: never tell a person they must keep their tariff type for 12 months.

Not verified: the date the change took effect in practice, and how E-REDES applies the
cycle-only permanence.

Sources:
- ERSE press release, 13 October 2025:
  https://www.erse.pt/media/3hidanjj/comunicado-regulamento-tarif%C3%A1rio.pdf
- Regulamento Tarifário do setor elétrico, ERSE consolidated text, January 2026 (article 54, n.º 5):
  https://www.erse.pt/media/5ewbseeb/articulado_rt-se_publicado-dr-com-dretif.pdf
- Diário da República entry for Regulamento n.º 1218/2025, as linked from that text:
  https://diariodarepublica.pt/dr/detalhe/regulamento/1218-2025-944873898

